      "name": "ReleaseFontBitmapTable",
      "signature": "void ReleaseFontBitmapTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Releases the font bitmap table memory allocated by CreateFontBitmapTable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if g_pbyFontBitmapData is non-NULL (bitmap table exists)\n  2. If exists, call ReleasePoolAllocation to free the 0x3000 (12288) byte buffer\n  3. Set g_pbyFontBitmapData to NULL to indicate table is released\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Safe to call if table was never created (NULL check prevents double-free)\n  - Counterpart to CreateFontBitmapTable which allocates g_pbyFontBitmapData",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:b249dc4e4339b300be453767366af27a",
