      "name": "DrawPixelLine",
      "signature": "void DrawPixelLine(int * pPointA, int * pPointB, undefined1 byColor)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draws a line from pPointA to pPointB on the render surface using fixed-point arithmetic\n  with Bresenham-style interpolation and boundary clipping.\n  \n  Algorithm:\n    1. Load start and end coordinates (X0, Y0) and (X1, Y1)\n    2. Calculate delta_x = X1 - X0 and delta_y = Y1 - Y0\n    3. If both deltas are 0, exit (single point = no line)\n    4. Compute line length: magnitude = sqrt(delta_x\u00b2 + delta_y\u00b2)\n    5. Scale deltas to 0x10000 fixed-point per unit: step_x = (delta_x << 0x10) / magnitude\n    6. Scale Y similarly: step_y = (delta_y << 0x10) / magnitude\n    7. Clip start point: iterate with fixed-point steps until entering screen bounds\n    8. For each valid pixel on the line:\n       - Accumulate X step, extract overflow into integer pixel offset\n       - Accumulate Y step, extract overflow into integer pixel offset\n       - Check bounds (0 <= X < width, 0 <= Y < height)\n       - Write color byte to render surface[Y * stride + X]\n       - Continue until line_length pixels plotted\n  \n  Parameters:\n    ECX (pPointA): Pointer to int[2] with X0, Y0 starting coordinates\n    EDX (pPointB): Pointer to int[2] with X1, Y1 ending coordinates\n    [ESP+4] (byColor): Pixel color (8-bit value written to surface)\n  \n  Returns:\n    void; uses RET 0x4 (caller pops 4-byte return address)\n  \n  Globals Referenced:\n    0x6f8f1784 (g_dwScreenHeight): Screen height in pixels\n    0x6f8f1b8c (g_dwScreenWidth): Screen width in pixels  \n    0x6f8f177c (g_dwRenderSurfaceLocked): Base address of locked render surface\n  \n  Special Cases:\n    - Skips if both delta_x and delta_y are 0\n    - Early clips and exits if start point outside bounds\n    - Exits if line extends outside screen after first pixel\n    - Handles negative step accumulation (SAR 0x10 for signed division)",
