      "name": "InitializeTileProjectDisplay",
      "signature": "void InitializeTileProjectDisplay(TileProject * pTileProj, dword nDisplayType)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes tile project display with specified display type mode\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Save ESI and EDI registers for preservation\n  2. Copy ECX (pTileProj) to ESI, EDX (nDisplayType) to EDI\n  3. Push initialization parameters (0x0, 0x1) onto stack\n  4. Call AllocateTileProjectBuffer(pTileProj) to allocate buffer\n  5. If allocation succeeds (EAX != 0):\n     - Calculate display offset based on nDisplayType (1, 2, or other)\n     - Type 1: Use g_dw1784 value, divide by 4 after sign extension\n     - Type 2: Use g_dw1784 value, negate then divide by 4\n     - Other: Use g_dw1784 value as base (type 0)\n     - Add calculated offset to ECX (base 0x50 offset)\n     - Retrieve function pointer from g_pfnDirectDrawRelease[0xc]\n     - Call function with (retaddr, nDisplayType, 0x1, 0x0)\n  6. Restore EDI and ESI registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  ECX: pTileProj - Pointer to TileProject structure to initialize\n  EDX: nDisplayType - Display type mode (0=default, 1=type1, 2=type2, other values use type1)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, modifies TileProject state via side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If AllocateTileProjectBuffer fails (returns 0), function returns immediately\n  - Display offset calculation uses sign extension and arithmetic right shift by 2 bits\n  - Modulo 4 operation (via AND 0x3) indicates alignment handling",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
