      "name": "ProcessVideoFrame",
      "signature": "void ProcessVideoFrame(void * pSmackContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes video frame data based on mode.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check mode flag at offset +0x4 (pSmackContext[1])\\n2. If mode == 'p': Apply palette color mapping to video buffer\\n   - Verify video disabled (DAT_6f8d0238 == 0) and buffer exists\\n   - Calculate destination offset using height, width, stride\\n   - Loop through 60 rows x 468 columns, applying palette lookup table\\n3. If mode == 's': Process Smacker video frame\\n   - Call SmackWait to check frame synchronization\\n   - If synchronized: Update palette from RGB data at +0x6d offset\\n   - Call SmackDoFrame to render frame\\n   - Check if video finished (offset +0x374 == offset +0xc)\\n   - Call SmackNextFrame to advance to next frame\\n4. If video flag enabled (DAT_6f8d01f8): Call FUN_6f8c8f10 to update display\\n\\nParameters:\\npSmackContext: SmackLib context structure (pointer to Smack context with video data and state)\\n  Accessed fields:\\n  - [0]: Video handle for SmackWait/SmackDoFrame\\n  - [4]: Mode flag ('p' for palette, 's' for smacker video)\\n  - [8]: Width value for display update\\n  - [12]: Frame offset for synchronization check\\n  - [60]: Palette update flag\\n  - [109]: RGB color data (3 bytes per color, up to 256 colors)\\n  - [372]: Current frame number\\n  - [876]: Total frame count\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Mode 'p': Applies 256-color palette mapping using lookup table at DAT_6f8cf680\\n- Palette update only occurs when SmackWait succeeds (frame synchronized)\\n- Color mapping uses FindClosestPaletteColor to convert RGB triplets to palette indices\\n- Video frame processing loops: 60 height x 468 width = 28,080 pixels per frame",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:1dd42338f7a8d5c0da4f672a0c14a2f3",
