      "name": "InitializeVideoOrPaletteRenderer",
      "signature": "void InitializeVideoOrPaletteRenderer(undefined4 fileId, int * pFileHandle, char renderMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes video rendering or palette data based on provided mode.\n\nHandles two primary workflows:\n1. Palette rendering (mode='p'): Extracts image file, converts RGB data to palette indices\n2. Smack video (mode='s'): Opens Smack video file and buffers first frame\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store render mode at pFileHandle+0x4 for later access\n2. If mode is 'p' (palette):\n   - Allocate palette buffer (0x53 bytes)\n   - Initialize buffer to zero (0x1b6c dwords)\n   - Extract file data from resource using ExtractFileToMemory\n   - Dispatch image format processing for RGB data\n   - Verify output dimensions match 0x1d4x0x3c with 8-bit depth\n   - Convert each RGB value to closest palette index\n   - Store indices in DAT_6f8cf680\n3. If mode is 's' (Smack):\n   - Skip if pFileHandle already has data\n   - Open Smack video file using _SmackOpen_12\n   - Allocate frame buffer (0x42 bytes)\n   - Clear buffer to zero\n   - Read first frame using _SmackToBuffer_28\n   - Set DAT_6f8d01f8 to 0\n4. On error or completion:\n   - Deallocate buffer via InitializeModule(0xf0)\n   - Close Smack file if open\n   - Reset pFileHandle to null\n\nParameters:\n- fileId: Resource file identifier\n- pFileHandle: File handle/state structure pointer\n- renderMode: 'p' for palette, 's' for Smack, else skip\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 0x1d4: Expected width (476 pixels)\n- 0x3c: Expected height (60 pixels)\n- 0x8: Expected depth (8-bit)\n- DAT_6f8cf780: Global image/video buffer\n- DAT_6f8cfdc8: Global 256-color palette\n- DAT_6f8cf680: Global output palette indices\n- DAT_6f8d01f8: Frame initialization flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
