      "name": "ValidateCoordinateBounds",
      "signature": "int ValidateCoordinateBounds(int coordinateIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates coordinate bounds within acceptable game world ranges.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Retrieve base value from validated structure field using first helper\\n2. Retrieve stride/scale value from structure field using null-check helper\\n3. If coordinateIndex is non-zero, adjust base and stride values:\\n   - Subtract stride from coordinateIndex (EBP = EBP - stride)\\n   - Add stride to base value (baseValue = baseValue + stride)\\n   - Divide stride by 2 for scaling (SAR ESI, 1)\\n4. Retrieve offset value from validated pointer field\\n5. Add offset to adjusted coordinate for absolute position\\n6. Validate absolute position against global upper bound at 0x6f8d01c8\\n7. Validate combined position against lower bound constraint (must be >= -1)\\n8. Retrieve additional field from pointer structure\\n9. Validate combined bounds against both global limits:\\n   - Upper bound: (combined + field - stride) < 0x6f8d01d8\\n   - Lower bound: (combined + field - stride) >= -1\\n10. Return 0 (success) if all bounds valid, 1 (failure) if any check fails\\n\\nParameters:\\n- coordinateIndex: int - Coordinate index for adjustment calculations\\n\\nReturns:\\n- int: 0 if all bounds validation passed, 1 if any bounds exceeded\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- coordinateIndex == 0: Skips stride adjustment calculations\\n- Negative values allowed if within lower bound constraint\\n- Multiple cascading bounds checks prevent overflow",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:13ddc20ad4f77f7e81ddc24e95416b41",
