      "name": "ProcessEntityWithDataClipping",
      "signature": "void ProcessEntityWithDataClipping(int pEntity, int dataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes an entity with data clipping validation and row processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize entity slots and validate initialization result\n2. Extract field pointer at offset +0x3c from entity\n3. Retrieve three field values from pointer using helper functions\n4. Calculate adjusted offset based on dataSize parameter\n5. Validate offset bounds against global limit (0x6f8d01c8)\n6. Validate cumulative offset doesn't overflow (negative check)\n7. Retrieve additional field and validate against threshold\n8. Calculate clipped index by dividing field by 2\n9. Validate processed index against global maximum (0x6f8d01d8)\n10. Check flag at offset +0x14 in global data structure\n11. Process clipped data rows with calculated parameters\n\nParameters:\n  pEntity: Pointer to entity structure (in ECX)\n  dataSize: Size or offset parameter (in EDX)\n\nReturns:\n  void (callee cleanup with RET 0x4)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if entity initialization fails\n  - Returns early if any bounds validation fails\n  - Conditional processing based on flag at global+0x14\n  - Uses global data structures at fixed addresses: 0x6f8d01c8, 0x6f8d01d0, etc.",
