      "name": "RenderValidatedEntityCel",
      "signature": "void RenderValidatedEntityCel(void * pEntity, int celOffsetY)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders a validated entity cel graphic with bounds checking.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize slot parameters (zeroParam=0, oneParam=1) on stack\\n2. Save entity pointer and cel offset to stack\\n3. Call InitializeEntityWithSlots to set up slot buffer\\n4. If initialization fails, skip rendering and return\\n5. Load entity graphics pointer from offset 0x3c\\n6. Call ValidateAndReturnStructField to get field value\\n7. Call GetStructFieldWithNullCheck for field value\\n8. Call GetFieldFromValidatedPointer to get graphics offset X\\n9. Check if (graphicsOffsetX + celOffsetY) fits within max bounds (DAT_6f8d01c8)\\n10. Check if result is not negative\\n11. Call ValidateAndGetPointerField for Y offset value\\n12. Check if (graphicsOffsetY + graphicsOffsetX) is not negative\\n13. Check if (graphicsOffsetY + graphicsOffsetX - unaff_ESI) fits within max height (DAT_6f8d01d8)\\n14. Call FUN_6f8c6a10 to prepare cel data\\n15. Call DrawCelRegionClipped to render the validated graphics region\\n16. Exit and cleanup stack\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pEntity - Pointer to entity/unit structure (passed in ECX)\\n  celOffsetY - Y offset for cel rendering (passed in EDX)\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void - Function performs rendering as side effect\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Returns early if InitializeEntityWithSlots fails (validation_failed)\\n  - Returns early if graphics offset exceeds bounds (x_bounds_exceeded, y_bounds_exceeded)\\n  - Returns early if graphics offset is negative (x_negative_check)\\n  - Returns early if dimensions exceed available space (dimensions_exceeded)\\n  - Stack cleanup: RET 0x10 (callee cleans up 2 parameters, 8 bytes each)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
