      "name": "InitializeLookupTableMapping",
      "signature": "void InitializeLookupTableMapping(uint * pSourceTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes lookup table mapping by copying source data, generating transformation values, and applying byte-level permutations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load floating-point parameter from global 0x6f8ceb90 for transformation initialization\n2. Copy 256 (0x100) dwords from pSourceTable to destination buffer at 0x6f8cf8b0\n3. Call GenerateFloatValuesIntoBuffer with parameters (floatParam=1, count=256, mask=0xff) to compute transformation values into local buffer\n4. Initialize loop counter to 0 (eax_index)\n5. Loop 1024 (0x400) times with 16-byte (0x10) stride:\n   - Load byte indices from source buffers at 0x6f8cf8b0-0x6f8cf8be\n   - Use indices to lookup transformed values in local buffer\n   - Store results to destination buffers at 0x6f8cfdc8, 0x6f8cfdcc, 0x6f8cfdd0, 0x6f8cfdd4, 0x6f8cfdd5, 0x6f8cfdd6\n   - Increment index by 16, check if less than 0x400, loop if true\n6. Set completion flag at 0x6f8d0240 to 1 indicating initialization complete\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceTable: Pointer to source data array (256 dwords), passed in ECX register\n\nReturns:\n  void: Modifies global state (output buffers and completion flag)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  The function processes exactly 256 input dwords and 1024 output bytes\n  Index 0xff is used as a mask parameter to GenerateFloatValuesIntoBuffer\n  Output is distributed across 6 separate buffers (0x6f8cfdc8, 0x6f8cfdcc, 0x6f8cfdd0, 0x6f8cfdd4, 0x6f8cfdd5, 0x6f8cfdd6)\n  Each output buffer receives a 16-byte aligned slice of the permuted data\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Buffer Name           Type     Description\n0x0000  0x100 SourceTable           uint[64] Input data array (256 dwords copied)\n0x0000  0x100 TransformedValues     byte[256] Lookup table for byte permutation\n0x0000  0x400 OutputBuffers         byte[1024] Permuted output split across 6 buffers",
