      "name": "ExitCriticalSection",
      "signature": "int ExitCriticalSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Exit a thread-safe critical section.\\n\\nThis function safely releases a critical section lock. It first attempts to unlock the section using a virtual method call. If unlocking fails, it logs an error and returns 0. Otherwise, it clears the global locked flag, invokes a cleanup handler, and attempts to leave the critical section. If the critical section is not initialized, it triggers error handling with GetReturnAddress and CleanupAndAbort. On successful exit, it leaves the critical section and returns 1.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load global object pointer from DAT_6f8d0220\\n2. Call virtual method at offset 0x80 (unlock handler)\\n3. If unlock fails (EAX != 0), log error message and return 0\\n4. Clear global lock flag (DAT_6f8cf8a8 = 0)\\n5. Call virtual method on DAT_6f8d01dc with parameters (0, 0)\\n6. Check if DAT_6f8d023c (CRITICAL_SECTION) is initialized\\n7. If not initialized, call GetReturnAddress(0x409) for debugging info\\n8. Call CleanupAndAbort with error string and return address\\n9. Call _exit(-1) to terminate\\n10. If critical section exists, call LeaveCriticalSection\\n11. Return 1 (success)\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone\\n\\nReturns:\\nint - Status code: 0 if unlock failed, 1 if critical section exited successfully\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- If the unlock handler (offset 0x80) fails, the function exits immediately with code 0\\n- If the critical section is not initialized, the function calls CleanupAndAbort which terminates the program\\n- Magic number 0x409: Standard error code for critical section initialization failure\\n- Magic number 0x80: Virtual method offset for unlock handler\\n- Magic number -0x1: Parameter to exit function, signal abnormal termination\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nGlobal object at DAT_6f8d0220 uses virtual method at offset 0x80 for unlock operations.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:fc018c069421e6c6c866ede8b3362ae4",
