      "name": "InitializeVideoConfiguration",
      "signature": "int InitializeVideoConfiguration(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes video configuration by reading registry settings and applying DirectDraw device fallback.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Verify system configuration is initialized via GetSystemConfigInitFlag()\\n2. If config not initialized, abort with error message and exit process\\n3. Check if video mode is set to 4 (if so, set global flag _DAT_6f8d01fc to 1)\\n4. Copy 5 configuration strings from global s_Diablo_II_VideoConfig into local buffers:\\n   - deviceNameBuffer (bytes 0-3)\\n   - flagsBuffer (bytes 4-7)\\n   - unknownBuffer1 (bytes 8-11)\\n   - unknownBuffer2 (bytes 12-15)\\n   - unknownBuffer3 (bytes 16-19)\\n   - unknownBuffer4 (bytes 20-21)\\n5. Query registry for device name using QueryRegistryData() - if successful, continue to step 6\\n6. Parse configuration flags using ParseConfigurationValue() - if successful, continue to step 7\\n7. Check if parsed flags match allowed bitmask (gdwBitMasks_exref) - if match found, return success (1)\\n8. Validate string parameters using ValidateAndProcessStringParameters() with buffer size 0x10\\n9. If validation passed and buffer size equals 0x10, return success (1)\\n10. If any step fails, apply fallback: copy 14 bytes from s_Fallback_DirectDraw_Device (6 DWORDs + 1 WORD + 1 BYTE)\\n11. Copy bitmask value from gdwBitMasks_exref to DAT_6f8cfcb0\\n12. Return success (1)\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone\\n\\nReturns:\\nint - Always returns 1 (success). Function handles all error cases internally via GetReturnAddress/CleanupAndAbort for early errors, or fallback device copy for registry/parsing failures.\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Early error at offset 0x6f8c888a: If GetSystemConfigInitFlag() returns 0, process exits with _exit(-1)\\n- Video mode check at offset 0x6f8c88ac: Special handling for mode 4 sets global flag\\n- Fallback at offset 0x6f8c896c: Applied if QueryRegistryData or ParseConfigurationValue fail, or if flags don't match bitmask\\n- Structure Layout: Configuration data copied in 4-byte chunks with buffer layout:\\n  Offset 0x0: Device name (4 bytes)\\n  Offset 0x4: Flags (4 bytes)\\n  Offset 0x8-0xF: Unknown buffers (12 bytes total)",
