      "comment": "Adapter function that saves context and delegates to core processing function.\\n\\nThis function acts as a wrapper that:\\n1. Saves the context parameter to a global storage location\\n2. Loads a data structure pointer\\n3. Tail-calls to the main processing function\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Store context parameter (ECX) to global DAT_6f8ceb94\\n2. Load address of data structure (0x6f8cf8b0) into ECX\\n3. Tail-call FUN_6f8c80c0 for main processing\\n\\nParameters:\\n  context: Context value passed via ECX register (fastcall convention)\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void: Delegates to FUN_6f8c80c0 via tail-call\\n\\nNote:\\n  This is a thin wrapper function that preserves a context value in global\\n  storage before invoking the main processing routine. The tail-call pattern\\n  means control never returns to this function.",
