      "name": "CleanupGraphicsResources",
      "signature": "void CleanupGraphicsResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Cleanup and release video graphics resources during shutdown.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if graphics system is initialized (DAT_6f8d0204)\\n2. If uninitialized, skip cleanup and exit\\n3. Loop 3 times:\\n   a. Initialize blit parameter buffer (19 DWORDs) with zeros\\n   b. Set blit timeout to 100 (offset +0x10 in buffer)\\n   c. Call blit manager vtable[0x14] to perform screen clear (blit operation)\\n   d. Check return value - if 0 (failed) or 0x887601ae (success)\\n   e. If success (0x887601ae): Calculate video buffer size (width * height)\\n      - Clear buffer using STOSD (dword fill) and STOSB (byte fill)\\n      - Process dwords first: size >> 2 iterations\\n      - Process remaining bytes: size & 3 iterations\\n   f. If failed (not 0x887601ae): Call error handler FUN_6f8c7690\\n   g. Call FUN_6f8c82f0 (post-blit cleanup)\\n4. Release three resource managers by calling vtable[0x8] destructor:\\n   - DAT_6f8d0220 (blit manager)\\n   - DAT_6f8d021c (second resource manager)\\n   - DAT_6f8d0218 (third resource manager)\\n5. Call cleanup function via DAT_6f8d01dc function pointer with params (0, 0)\\n6. Mark graphics as uninitialized: set DAT_6f8d0204=0, DAT_6f8d0208=0\\n7. Return (RET with no stack cleanup per __stdcall)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Blit return value 0x887601ae is success sentinel for graphics operation\\n- Loop executes exactly 3 times for triple-buffering or triple-clearing\\n- Remainder byte clearing after dword clearing uses AND 0x3 pattern\\n- All resource cleanup must occur regardless of blit success/failure\\n- Function zeros both DAT_6f8d0204 (initialized flag) and DAT_6f8d0208 (shadow flag)\\n\\nMemory Layout - Blit Parameter Buffer (19 DWORDs = 76 bytes):\\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type     Description\\n0x00    0x4c  blitBuffer[0-18]     uint[19] Blit operation parameters\\n0x10    0x4   timeout              uint     Blit timeout value (100)\\n---\\nTotal: 76 bytes (0x6c), allocated on stack as local_6c\\n\\nGlobals:\\nDAT_6f8d0204 - Graphics initialized flag (1=ready, 0=shutdown)\\nDAT_6f8d0208 - Graphics shadow/secondary flag\\nDAT_6f8d0220 - Blit manager object (vtable at [0x0], destructor at [0x8], method at [0x14])\\nDAT_6f8d021c - Resource manager #2\\nDAT_6f8d0218 - Resource manager #3\\nDAT_6f8d01d8 - Video buffer width\\nDAT_6f8d01c8 - Video buffer height\\nDAT_6f8cf8a8 - Video buffer base pointer\\nDAT_6f8d01dc - Cleanup function pointer",
