      "name": "PlayBinkCutsceneVideo",
      "signature": "void PlayBinkCutsceneVideo(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Plays a Bink video cutscene with proper initialization, audio setup, and message handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if cutscene already initialized or external stop requested\n2. Initialize Bink video library by getting DirectSound surface type\n3. Set Bink sound system to use DirectSound audio\n4. Query game configuration state for quality level (0=unset, 1-3=quality levels)\n5. Open video file and get file handle for Bink playback\n6. If file open fails, clean up and return\n7. Select Bink open flags based on quality level:\n   - Default: 0x800000 (quality 0)\n   - Quality 1: 0x30800000\n   - Quality 2: 0x10800000\n   - Quality 3: 0x40800000\n8. Open Bink file with selected quality flags\n9. If Bink open fails, close file and return\n10. Calculate video dimensions from Bink frame header:\n    - Video height: (DAT_6f8d01c8 - first_dword) / 2\n    - Align height to 4-byte boundary if needed\n    - Video width: (DAT_6f8d01d8 - second_dword) / 2\n11. Enter main playback loop with GetTickCount() baseline\n12. Loop continues while: stop flag=0 AND timeout hasn't expired AND external stop not set\n13. Each frame iteration:\n    - Call user callback if provided (can exit via exitPressedFlag)\n    - Peek for Windows messages (keyboard/mouse input)\n    - Check for specific window messages:\n      - 0x12 (WM_QUIT): Set stop flags and timestamp\n      - 0x102 (WM_CHAR): Set stop flags and timestamp\n      - 0x201 (WM_LBUTTONDOWN): Set exit flag and timestamp\n      - 0x204/0x207 (WM_RBUTTONDOWN/WM_MBUTTONDOWN): Set exit flag and timestamp\n      - Others: Just translate and dispatch\n    - If no message, check if Bink frame ready:\n      - If ready: call FUN_6f8c6ff0 to render frame\n      - If not ready: Sleep(1ms) to yield CPU\n14. When loop exits, check if user requested exit via stop flag\n15. Close Bink file and file handle\n16. If user initiated exit (stop flag set), call _exit(-1) for forced termination\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Timeout: 500ms after initial frame load\n- Audio reset called twice (before and after Bink close)\n- RET 0xc indicates 3 stack parameters passed by caller\n- Uses global variables for state management (DAT_6f8d0244=Bink handle, DAT_6f8d0250=stop flag)\n- Message loop may be interrupted by external process termination signal",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
