      "name": "ProcessObjectsInBounds",
      "signature": "int ProcessObjectsInBounds(void * pRegion, uint boundsMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes all objects within spatial bounds and applies callback handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize network cache pool with region data\n2. Calculate bounding box coordinates based on mode parameter\n   - Mode 0: Full bounds (max Y = DAT_6f8d01d8 + 0x20, min Y = -0x20)\n   - Mode 1: Half bounds (divide X by 2, keep full Y range)\n   - Mode 2: Half bounds offset (divide X by 2, offset min Y by -0x20)\n3. Iterate through all objects in region (count at offset +0x50)\n4. For each object, load X,Y coordinates from position array at offset +0x54\n5. Add base offsets (baseXOffset in ESI, baseYOffset in stack) to object coordinates\n6. Validate object position within calculated bounds\n7. If within bounds, extract color indices from color map using X coordinate >> 5\n8. Call handler function at DAT_6f8d01dc + 0x10 with Y coordinate and color data\n9. Return 1 if any objects processed, 0 if none or cache init failed\n\nParameters:\n  pRegion (ECX) - Pointer to region/sector object\n    +0x50: Count of objects in this region\n    +0x54: Pointer to array of object position data\n  boundsMode (EDX) - Processing mode flag (0=full, 1/2=half bounds variant)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Successfully processed at least one object within bounds\n  0 - No objects processed or cache initialization failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses unaffected registers ESI and stack for base offset values\n  - Color map accessed with stride of 4 bytes per X/32 coordinate\n  - Bounds check includes all four conditions (x_min, x_max, y_min, y_max)\n  - Coordinate data is stored as signed shorts in object position array\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type        Description\n  0x50    4     objectCount     dword       Number of objects in region\n  0x54    4     pPositionArray  pointer     Points to array of position data",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
