      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.12a": 1039,
        "LoD/1.13c": 1039,
        "LoD/PD2": 1039
      },
      "name": "ConvertDecimalStringToLargeNumber",
      "signature": "void ConvertDecimalStringToLargeNumber(uint * pResultNumber, int * pEndPos, byte * pInputString, int decimalExponent, int scaleFactor, int integralExponent, int allowExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Parses a decimal string into a normalized large number structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace (space, tab, newline, carriage return)\n2. Parse optional sign character ('+' or '-')\n3. Transition to appropriate state based on character type (digit, decimal, null)\n4. State 3 (Integral digits): collect significant digits into buffer, track overflow\n5. State 4 (Decimal digits): skip leading zeros, collect fractional digits, adjust exponent\n6. State 6 (Exponent marker): handle D/E/d/e character markers\n7. State 7-9 (Exponent value): parse optional exponent sign and numeric value\n8. Handle zero prefix normalization: skip leading/trailing zeros, adjust exponent downward\n9. Trim overflow digits from buffer (max 24 digits), apply rounding if digit >= 5\n10. Normalize digit buffer to large number via ParseDecimalString\n11. Calculate final exponent: combine decimal position + parsed exponent \u00b1 integral/decimal adjustments\n12. Check exponent bounds: must be between -5201 and 5201 (0xffffebb0 to 0x1450)\n13. Scale mantissa via MultiplyLargeNumber: apply final exponent to mantissa\n14. Store result structure: mantissa low word + mantissa high dword + exponent + sign flags\n\nParameters:\npResultNumber - Pointer to 12-byte result structure (mantissa: 6 bytes, exponent: 4 bytes, sign: 2 bytes)\npEndPos - Pointer to output: final position in input string after parsing\npInputString - Pointer to null-terminated input decimal string to parse\ndecimalExponent - Exponent adjustment for decimal point (scale factor)\nscaleFactor - Additional exponent scaling for results without decimal point\nintegralExponent - Exponent adjustment when integral part is present\nallowExponent - Flag: 0=disable E/D exponent markers, nonzero=enable\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result written to pResultNumber structure via pointer:\n  Offset 0x0: mantissa low word (undefined2)\n  Offset 0x2: mantissa high dword (undefined4)\n  Offset 0x6: exponent value (undefined4)\n  Offset 0xA: sign and status flags (undefined2, upper bits contain sign)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Leading zeros: Stored as negative exponent adjustment, not in digit buffer\n- Decimal without digits: Treated as 0.0\n- Exponent overflow (>5201): Sets overflow status (0x7fff mantissa + 0x80000000 exponent)\n- Exponent underflow (<-5201): Returns zero (0 mantissa + 0 exponent)\n- Non-numeric input: Returns zero value\n- Rounding: Applied when buffer contains >24 digits and overflow digit >= 5\n- All zeros detected: Treated as zero value\n- Stack canary verification: Compares XOR guard before/after to detect buffer overflows\n\nStructure Layout (Output):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type      Description\n------  ----  ---------------------   --------  -----------------------\n0x0     2     mantissaLow             uint16    Low word of 48-bit mantissa\n0x2     4     mantissaHigh            uint32    High dword of 48-bit mantissa\n0x6     4     exponentValue           int32     Adjusted exponent (-5201 to 5201)\n0xA     2     signAndStatus           uint16    Sign bit in 0x8000, status in lower bits",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
