      "name": "ConvertFloatingPointToDecimalString",
      "signature": "void ConvertFloatingPointToDecimalString(uint mantissaLow, uint mantissaHigh, ushort exponent, int precision, byte flags, short * pOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts an IEEE 754 extended-precision floating-point number to decimal string representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize carry buffer (12 bytes) with sentinel values (0xcc, 0xfb, 0x3f)\n2. Extract and set sign bit from exponent bit 15 to output[1] (0x20 positive, 0x2d negative)\n3. Check for zero: if mantissa==0 AND exp==0, write \"0\" to output and return\n4. Check for special exponent value 0x7fff:\n   - If mantissa==0: write \"INF\" or \"-INF\" based on sign\n   - If mantissa!=0 with bit 30 set: write \"SNAN\" for signaling NaN\n   - If mantissa!=0 with bit 30 clear: write \"QNAN\" for quiet NaN\n   - If specific pattern (exponent=0x7fff, mantissa=0xc0000000): write \"IND\" for indeterminate\n5. For normal numbers, calculate internal exponent using formula: ((exp >> 8) + (mantissa_high >> 24)*2)*0x4d + offset*0x4d10\n6. Normalize mantissa by scaling: left-shift by 8 positions, then right-shift if needed for denormalized\n7. Generate decimal digits in precision+1 iterations: shift mantissa left 3 bits, add to carry, shift left again\n8. Extract high byte of carry buffer as ASCII digit (carryBuf1f - 0xfb = decimal digit)\n9. Apply rounding: if last digit >= '5' round up with carry propagation, else truncate trailing zeros\n10. Write result structure: exponent(2 bytes) | sign(1 byte) | digitCount(1 byte) | digits | null terminator\n11. Verify stack canary before return\n\nParameters:\n  mantissaLow: Low 32 bits of 64-bit IEEE 754 mantissa\n  mantissaHigh: High 32 bits of IEEE 754 mantissa with sign bit in bit 15 of exponent parameter\n  exponent: 16-bit exponent field where bit 15 = sign, bits 0-14 = biased exponent (0x3fff bias)\n  precision: Number of decimal digits to generate (clamped to 0-21 range)\n  flags: Bit 0 set = add exponent to precision for adjusted conversion mode\n  pOutputBuffer: Pointer to output structure containing exponent, sign, digit count, and digit string\n\nReturns:\n  None (results written directly to pOutputBuffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero: mantissa==0 and exponent==0, returns \"0\" with exponent=0 and length=1\n  - Positive infinity: exponent==0x7fff and mantissa==0 and sign=0, returns \"INF\"\n  - Negative infinity: exponent==0x7fff and mantissa==0 and sign=1, returns \"-INF\"\n  - Quiet NaN: exponent==0x7fff and mantissa!=0 with bit 30 clear, returns \"QNAN\"\n  - Signaling NaN: exponent==0x7fff and mantissa!=0 with bit 30 set, returns \"SNAN\"\n  - Indeterminate: exponent==0x7fff and mantissa==0xc0000000, returns \"IND\"\n  - Denormalized: exponent==0 with mantissa!=0, treated as very small normal number\n  - Rounding overflow: if rounding causes mantissa overflow, exponent incremented by 1\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name         Type      Description\n  0       2     exponent           word      Biased exponent value\n  2       1     signByte           byte      0x20 (positive) or 0x2d (negative)\n  3       1     digitCount         byte      Number of decimal digits in string\n  4       n     digits             char[n]   ASCII digit characters 0-9\n  4+n     1     null               byte      Null terminator",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.12a",
