      "name": "FillOrBlitVideoRegion",
      "signature": "void FillOrBlitVideoRegion(uint startColumn, uint startRow, uint endColumn, uint endRow, byte fillColor, int operation)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Fills or copies a rectangular region of video memory with clipping and mode selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6f8c6a10 to get color lookup offset based on startColumn\n2. Clamp startColumn and endColumn to valid video bounds (0 to MAX_VIDEO_WIDTH-1)\n3. Clamp startRow and endRow to valid video bounds (0 to MAX_VIDEO_HEIGHT-1)\n4. Validate that clamped values don't cause invalid memory access\n5. Dispatch based on operation mode:\n   - Mode 1: Copy pixels using color lookup table indexed by offset\n   - Mode 2: Fill region with solid fillColor value\n   - Mode 0/other: Fill region with repeated fillColor pattern (32-bit aligned)\n6. Calculate destination video memory pointer as: videoBase[startRow * stride] + clampedStartCol\n7. For each row in region, apply operation to each pixel/dword in row\n8. Return when all rows processed\n\nParameters:\n- startColumn: Starting column index (will be clamped to video bounds)\n- startRow: Starting row index (will be clamped to video bounds)\n- endColumn: Ending column index (exclusive, will be clamped)\n- endRow: Ending row index (exclusive, will be clamped)\n- fillColor: Color byte value used in fill operations\n- operation: Operation mode (1=indexed copy, 2=solid fill, other=pattern fill)\n\nReturns:\n- void: Modifies video memory in-place, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative or out-of-bounds coordinates are clamped to valid range\n- Region is clipped to video dimensions (DAT_6f8d01c8 = max width, DAT_6f8d01d8 = max height)\n- If clamped bounds become invalid (start >= end after clamping), triggers error handler\n- Mode 2 fill is optimized for single-byte operations\n- Mode 0/other fill is optimized using 32-bit operations with manual tail byte handling\n- Video memory stride is DAT_6f8d01c8 bytes per row\n- Video base address is DAT_6f8cf8a8",
