      "name": "InitializeDisplayDimensions",
      "signature": "void InitializeDisplayDimensions(bool bUseHighResolution)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes display resolution parameters based on graphics capability.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Clear the display mode flag by writing 0 to the mode field\\n2. Set initial height to 0x280 (640 pixels) as default resolution\\n3. If high-resolution mode is requested (bUseHighResolution != 0):\\n   - Override height to 0x320 (800 pixels) for higher resolution display\\n4. Return after configuration\\n\\nParameters:\\n  bUseHighResolution: bool flag (CL register) indicating whether to use high-resolution mode\\n    - false/0: Use standard resolution (640 pixels height)\\n    - true/non-zero: Use high resolution (800 pixels height)\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void: No return value; function modifies global display configuration variables\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - The function always clears the mode flag first (0x6f8d01e8 = 0)\\n  - Default resolution is 640px, overridden to 800px when flag is set\\n  - Magic numbers: 0x280 = 640, 0x320 = 800 (likely pixel heights)\\n  - Called during DirectDraw video initialization\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\n  Global Display Configuration:\\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\\n  ------  ----  -----------------    -----   --------------------------------------------------\\n  0x00    4     DisplayModeFlag      uint    Mode/state flag (cleared to 0)\\n  0x04    4     DisplayHeight        uint    Height in pixels (0x280 or 0x320)\\n  \\nNote: This function configures global display parameters used by rendering functions\\n(ProcessEntityWithDataClipping, RenderEntityCelWithBoundsCheck, RenderValidatedEntityCel)",
