      "name": "GetCelPropertyByMode",
      "signature": "uint GetCelPropertyByMode(uint modeIndex, uint * pPropertyTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves cel rendering properties from a mode-indexed lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate modeIndex is in range [0, 6] by comparing with 6\n2. Load offset value from mode-indexed table at DAT_6f8ceb98[modeIndex * 4]\n3. Store offset value to output parameter pPropertyTable\n4. Jump to appropriate case handler based on modeIndex value\n5. For each case (0-4, 6): Load property from DAT_6f8cf784 at computed offset\n6. Return retrieved property value in EAX\n7. For invalid modes (5 and above): Return 0\n\nParameters:\n- modeIndex (EAX): Mode index value [0-6] selects which property to retrieve\n- pPropertyTable (EDX): Pointer to output uint where offset table entry is stored\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Property value from DAT_6f8cf784 at offset based on modeIndex, or 0 for invalid modes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode 0: Returns DAT_6f8cf784[0x2]\n- Mode 1: Returns DAT_6f8cf784[0x1]\n- Mode 2: Returns DAT_6f8cf784[0]\n- Mode 3: Returns DAT_6f8cf784[0x41]\n- Mode 4: Returns DAT_6f8cf784[0x42]\n- Mode 6: Returns DAT_6f8cf784[0x43]\n- Mode 5 and others: Returns 0",
