      "name": "ValidateEntityPositionInBounds",
      "signature": "undefined4 ValidateEntityPositionInBounds(void * pUnit, int yOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates all entity positions within game map bounds and invokes callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize network cache pool for entity data structures\n2. Load map boundary configuration based on game mode/difficulty\n3. Calculate X and Y boundary limits with mode-specific offsets\n4. Iterate through all entities in the entity array (stride = 0x14 bytes)\n5. For each entity: load X,Y coordinates from entity structure (offsets +0, +2)\n6. Apply X,Y coordinate offsets from parameters\n7. Validate: xMin <= x < xMax AND yMin <= y < yMax (bounds: [-32, 32])\n8. If valid: set result flag=1, invoke callback with Y-coordinate or with flag 0xc0\n9. Advance loop counter and continue until all entities processed\n10. Return result flag (1=valid, 0=invalid/init_failed)\n\nParameters:\npUnit [ECX]: Pointer to unit/entity container structure\n  +0x50: uint - entity count (loop bound)\n  +0x54: int* - entity data array pointer\nyOffset [EDX]: int - Y coordinate offset to apply during validation\n\nReturns:\nundefined4 (in EAX): 1 if at least one entity passed bounds check, 0 otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Game mode 0: standard bounds, X_min = -32\n- Game mode 1: reduced bounds, X_max = width/2\n- Game mode 2: expanded bounds, X_min = width/2 - 32\n- Entity stride is 0x14 (20) bytes\n- Y bounds fixed: -33 to (y_max+32)\n- Callbacks stored in vtable: offset +4 (simple), offset +0x14 (with flags)\n- All coordinates are 16-bit signed integers\n- Callback type determined by DAT_6f8d01d0[0x14]",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a1fd4898b42622c1fd8324dbe77dd0a1",
