      "name": "InitializeCutsceneSurface",
      "signature": "void InitializeCutsceneSurface(int * pVideoSystem, int nParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a cutscene video surface by allocating a buffer and calling the video system's surface creation method.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if surface is already initialized (DAT_6f8d0238)\n2. If not initialized, allocate local buffer (76 bytes) with capacity 100\n3. Zero-initialize buffer array (24 DWORD elements)\n4. Set initialization flag (DAT_6f8d020c = 1)\n5. Validate video system pointer (DAT_6f8d0218 != NULL)\n6. Call virtual method [video_system + 0x14] with parameters: buffer address, 0x400 flag, capacity\n7. Check if surface creation succeeded (return value != NULL)\n8. If failure, call error handler FUN_6f8c7690 and return\n9. If success, call FUN_6f8c70e0 and clear initialization flag\n10. Return with 4-byte parameter cleanup (__stdcall)\n\nParameters:\n- pVideoSystem (ECX, __stdcall implicit): Video system object pointer\n- nParam (EDX, __stdcall implicit): Additional parameter value\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function does not return a value\n- Sets global flag DAT_6f8d020c to indicate initialization state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x384 (900 decimal) passed to GetReturnAddress for error tracking\n- Magic number 0x400 flag used for video surface creation\n- Local buffer capacity is hardcoded to 100\n- If video system pointer is NULL, calls CleanupAndAbort and exits with -1\n- Function clears initialization flag after successful setup\n\nStructure Layout:\nUsed for surface buffer initialization - 76 byte allocation on stack:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Purpose\n0x0c   | 0x4  | capacity   | int  | Surface buffer capacity (100)\n0x10   | 0x4c | buffer     | int[19] | Surface configuration/state buffer",
